{#
    Alternatives as a horizontal card rail, the cross-selling pattern Shopware's own
    storefront uses, which this audience reads without being taught.

    Deliberately a scroll-snap rail rather than a JavaScript carousel. Every card is
    in the DOM and reachable: it scrolls with the trackpad, with shift+wheel, by
    tabbing through the links, and by dragging on touch. Nothing is hidden behind a
    control, nothing auto-advances, and it works with JavaScript disabled. The arrow
    buttons are an enhancement on top, not the mechanism.

    That matters more here than on a shop. A carousel that hides two thirds of its
    contents is an annoyance when it is selling socks and a real obstacle when
    somebody is deciding which payment plugin to put in production.
#}
<div class="rail" data-controller="rail">
    <div class="rail-track" data-rail-target="track" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Alternative extensions">
        {% for alternative in alternatives %}
            <article class="alt-card">
                {{ include('catalog/_icon.html.twig', {extension: alternative.extension}) }}
                <a class="alt-card-title" href="{{ path('extension_detail', {slug: alternative.extension.slug}) }}">
                    {{ alternative.extension.label }}
                </a>
                <span class="alt-card-package">{{ alternative.extension.packageName }}</span>

                {% if alternative.declaredVersions %}
                    <div class="alt-card-versions">
                        {% for version in alternative.declaredVersions %}
                            <span class="chip chip--version is-explicit">{{ version }}</span>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                {% endif %}

                <p class="alt-card-why">{{ alternative.reasons|join(' · ') }}</p>

                <div class="alt-card-foot">
                    <span class="chip {{ alternative.extension.licenseStatus.value in ['unknown', 'rejected'] ? 'chip--risk' : '' }}">
                        {{ alternative.extension.licenseSpdx ?? alternative.extension.licenseStatus.badgeLabel }}
                    </span>
                    {% if alternative.extension.lastCommitAt %}
                        <span class="small muted num">{{ alternative.extension.lastCommitAt|ago }}</span>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            </article>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {# Hidden until the controller confirms the track actually overflows, arrows on a
       rail that already fits are furniture that does nothing. #}
    <button class="rail-nav rail-nav--prev" type="button" hidden
            data-rail-target="prev" data-action="rail#prev" aria-label="Scroll to previous alternatives">‹</button>
    <button class="rail-nav rail-nav--next" type="button" hidden
            data-rail-target="next" data-action="rail#next" aria-label="Scroll to more alternatives">›</button>
</div>
